<doc>Pre-processing rules applied before parsing to keep payload deterministic and avoid parser pollution.</doc>
INSTRUCTION HYGIENE:
Remove all <doc>…</doc> blocks from input payload before parsing (byte-stream safe).
Remove all <doc>…</doc> blocks within CONFIGURATION section before parsing.

Treat every CONFIGURATION assignment whose resolved value is an empty
string as undefined.

Do not serialize undefined settings.

A module or container whose controlling ID is undefined must not be
created. Do not evaluate that module's nested mapping instructions.

Inside a collection loop, skip entries whose required configuration
values are undefined. Optional object properties may be omitted
individually.

<doc>Here you define how post-its should be treated when extracted. So any change regarding that should (if possible) always placed here instead of at module level.</doc>
For all post-it extractions:
    Only extract text from actual handwritten square post-its.
    Post-its are square with a general standard size of 3x3 inches.
    All post-its are handwritten.
    Detect every individual post-it in the read area and extract each one separately.
    If multiple post-its are present in one read area, process them in top-to-bottom, then left-to-right order.
    Only extract text written inside the borders of the post-it.
    Ignore any printed board text, template text, headings, labels, legends, axis text, rating-scale text, octagon text, connector lines, or any other non-post-it content, even if it appears inside, near, or overlapping the read area.
    The read area defines where to search for post-its, not which non-post-it text to extract.
    Preserve the original wording of each post-it.
    Apply only light normalization: correct obvious typos, normalize case, and remove line-break hyphenation.
    Do not summarize, reinterpret, merge, or paraphrase.
    If text is only partially legible, extract all legible text line by line and leave uncertain or incomplete text unresolved rather than guessing.
    If a post-it is only partially legible, perform a second pass on a tighter crop of that individual post-it before final extraction.
    If any extracted post-it text appears truncated, incomplete, or low-confidence, re-inspect that exact post-it in a tighter crop before returning the final result.
    Only keep text incomplete if the second pass still does not make the missing part legible.

<doc>Normalize page orientation and geometry before applying any module-specific read areas.</doc>
For every PDF page or image used for visual extraction:

    Render the complete page as an image.

    Create four orientation candidates:
        Candidate 01 = original orientation
        Candidate 02 = rotated 90 degrees clockwise
        Candidate 03 = rotated 180 degrees
        Candidate 04 = rotated 90 degrees counterclockwise

    Evaluate every candidate using:
        horizontal text-line orientation
        OCR confidence for printed headings
        expected module-specific headings
        expected position and order of rows and columns
        expected placement of logos, title bars, side banners, and
        table headers
        consistency of visible horizontal and vertical grid lines

    Do not select an orientation from OCR confidence alone.

    Select the candidate that produces the strongest consistent match
    with the module-specific layout anchors.

    If two candidates remain equally plausible:
        Do not extract or map post-its from that page.
        Report the page as having ambiguous orientation.

    Record:
        {DETECTED_SOURCE_ROTATION}
        {APPLIED_CORRECTION_ROTATION}
        {ORIENTATION_CONFIDENCE}
        {ORIENTATION_ANCHORS_FOUND}

    Set:
        {NORMALIZED_PAGE_IMAGE}
            = page image after applying the selected correction

    After rotation normalization:
        Detect the outer document, poster, board, or table boundary.

        If perspective distortion or camera skew is present:
            Deskew or perspective-correct the relevant document area.
            Preserve the relative positions of rows, columns, grid
            lines, post-its, and printed labels.

        Set:
            {NORMALIZED_DOCUMENT_IMAGE}
                = corrected document image used for extraction

    Apply all module-specific coordinates, top/bottom relationships,
    left/right relationships, and read areas only to
    {NORMALIZED_DOCUMENT_IMAGE}.

    Never apply module-specific coordinates to the unnormalized source
    image.


TOOLS:
<doc>This is a method to generate unique IDs for objects in a consistent and deterministic way.</doc>
{METHOD_ID_GENERATOR}({namespace}, {input}):
    Normalize: trim whitespace, lowercase, apply Unicode NFC.
    Concatenate namespace and string as "{namespace}|{input}".
    Hash with SHA‑256.
    Take the first 8 bytes as a big‑endian unsigned integer.
    Compute modulo 10^12, zero‑pad to 12 digits.
    Namespace: {namespace}
    Input: {input}
    Checksum: none (use all 12 digits for data).
    Output format: return 12-digit string.


<doc>Use this section to define the main configurations and also the metrics for the files where the information should be extracted from.</doc>
CONFIGURATION:

{JSON_SCHEMA} = "ws_classes.schema.json" <doc>we are still using the JSON schema as reference for the structure to use.</doc>
<doc>Global runtime constants used for extraction and ID generation across all modules.</doc>
{CUSTOMER_NAME} = "IPCO"
{TARGET_FILE} = lower({CUSTOMER_NAME}) + „_ws_results.json“
{COMMON_ABBREVIATIONS} = "KI, HCM, SAP"
{ABBREVIATION_CORRECTIONS} = "HCL->HCM, S.A.P->SAP, K.I->KI"

{WORKSHOP_DATE} = "2026-10-01"

If {TARGET_FILE} already contains objects of type PostIt:
     {NOTE_COUNTER} = max(PostIt.id in {TARGET_FILE}) 
Else:
    {NOTE_COUNTER} = 0

<doc>Input file(s) for Free Association module.</doc>
{MD_FREE_ASSOCIATION_FILE} = "IPCO/BusinessServitization/IPCO_Sevitization_Brainstorming.pdf"

<doc>Input file(s) for Different Views with Ratings module. Here the naming is important and has to be updated also in the EXECUTION section.</doc>
{CT_DIFF_VIEWS_RATED_FILE_SALES} = ""
{CT_DIFF_VIEWS_RATED_FILE_DELIVERY} = ""
{CT_DIFF_VIEWS_RATED_FILE_MANAGEMENT} = ""

<doc>Input file(s) for Capability Matrix module.</doc>
{MD_CAPABILITY_MATRIX_FILE} = ""

<doc>Input file(s) for Value Effort Matrix module.</doc>
{CT_VALUE_EFFORT_MATRIX_FILE} = "IPCO/BusinessServitization/IPCO_Sevitization_ValueMatrix.pdf"

<doc>Input file(s) for Detailed Working Plan module. Here the naming is important and has to be updated also in the EXECUTION section.</doc>
{CT_DETAILED_WORKING_PLAN_FILE_TEAM_RED} = ""
{CT_DETAILED_WORKING_PLAN_FILE_TEAM_GREEN} = ""
{CT_DETAILED_WORKING_PLAN_FILE_TEAM_BLUE} = ""

<doc>Input file(s) for User Journey module.</doc>
{CT_USER_JOURNEY_FILE} = ""

<doc>Input file(s) for Detailed Idea plus Investment module.</doc>
{CT_DETAILED_IDEA_INVESTMENT_FILE} = ""

<doc>Input file(s) for Roadmap module.</doc>
{MD_ROADMAP_FILE} = ""

<doc>Input file(s) for Staged Offering Portfolio module.</doc>
{MD_STAGED_OFFERING_PORTFOLIO_FILE} = ""

<doc>Input file(s) for Scenario Summary module.</doc>
{CT_SCENARIO_SUMMARY_FILE} = ""

<doc>Input file(s) for Different Scenarios Rated module.</doc>
{CT_DIFF_SCENARIOS_RATED_FILE} = "IPCO/BusinessServitization/IPCO_Servitization_LevelRating.pdf"

<doc>Input file(s) for Module LifeCycle module.</doc>
{MD_LIFE_CYCLE_FILE} = "IPCO/BusinessServitization/IPCO_Servitization_LifeCycle.pdf"

<doc>Input file(s) for Advanced User Journey module.</doc>
{CT_ADVANCED_USER_JOURNEY_FILE} = "IPCO/BusinessServitization/IPCO_Servitization_Roadmap.pdf"


<doc>Here you only update the already exting {TARGET_FILE} that has been created in the 'prefill' step. We use the properties of {TARGET_FILE} directly to clearly instruct the LLM for mapping.</doc>
EXECUTION:

Structure for the data mapping = {JSON_SCHEMA}:


<doc>Populate the existing Module_LifeCycle from the configured
lifecycle poster.</doc>
If {MD_LIFE_CYCLE_FILE} is not empty:

    Read out all hand-written post-its from {MD_LIFE_CYCLE_FILE}

    Map the extracted content to {TARGET_FILE}.module_LifeCycle while taking the structure of {JSON_SCHEMA} into consideration.
    

<doc>Populate Free Association by reading all post-its in the configured area and appending as PostIt notes.</doc>
If {MD_FREE_ASSOCIATION_FILE} is not empty:

    Read out all hand-written post-its from {MD_FREE_ASSOCIATION_FILE}

    Map the extracted content to {TARGET_FILE}.module_FreeAssociation while taking the structure of {JSON_SCHEMA} into consideration.
    

<doc>Populate Different Views Rated by pairing idea/problem rows and attaching category ratings by column alignment.</doc>
If at least one of {CT_DIFF_VIEWS_RATED_FILE_XX} is not empty:

    For each {CT_DIFF_VIEWS_RATED_FILE_XX}:
        
        Read out all hand-written post-its

        Map the extracted content to {TARGET_FILE}.container_DifferentViewsRated while taking the structure of {JSON_SCHEMA} into consideration.


<doc>Enrich capability entries with rating and extracted supporting post-it notes per capability area.</doc>
If {MD_CAPABILITY_MATRIX_FILE} is not empty:
    
    Read out all hand-written post-its from {MD_CAPABILITY_MATRIX_FILE}

    Map the extracted content to {TARGET_FILE}.module_CapabilityMatrix while taking the structure of {JSON_SCHEMA} into consideration.
        

<doc>Populate Value/Effort modules per team and classify each extracted idea into a weight category based on location.</doc>
If {CT_VALUE_EFFORT_MATRIX_FILE} is not empty:

    Read out all hand-written post-its from {CT_VALUE_EFFORT_MATRIX_FILE}

    Map the extracted content to {TARGET_FILE}.container_ValueEffortMatrix while taking the structure of {JSON_SCHEMA} into consideration.
      

<doc>Populate Detailed Working Plan per team, including Big Bet and notes for explanation/resource sections.</doc>
If at least one of {CT_DETAILED_WORKING_PLAN_FILE_TEAM_XX} is not empty:

    For each {CT_DETAILED_WORKING_PLAN_FILE_TEAM_XX}:
        
        Read out all hand-written post-its

        Map the extracted content to {TARGET_FILE}.container_DetailedWorkingPlan while taking the structure of {JSON_SCHEMA} into consideration.


<doc>Populate User Journey step notes by matching extracted post-its to nearby journey step descriptions.</doc>
If {CT_USER_JOURNEY_FILE} is not empty:

    Read out all hand-written post-its from {CT_USER_JOURNEY_FILE}

    Map the extracted content to {TARGET_FILE}.container_UserJourney while taking the structure of {JSON_SCHEMA} into consideration.


<doc>Populate Advanced User Journey step notes by matching extracted post-its to nearby journey step descriptions.</doc>
If {CT_ADVANCED_USER_JOURNEY_FILE} is not empty:

    Read out all hand-written post-its from {CT_ADVANCED_USER_JOURNEY_FILE}

    Map the extracted content to {TARGET_FILE}.container_AdvancedUserJourney while taking the structure of {JSON_SCHEMA} into consideration.
   

<doc>Populate Staged Offering Portfolio streams by matching extracted post-its to reading areas.</doc>
If {MD_STAGED_OFFERING_PORTFOLIO_FILE} is not empty:
    
    Read out all hand-written post-its from {MD_STAGED_OFFERING_PORTFOLIO_FILE}

    Map the extracted content to {TARGET_FILE}.module_StagedOfferingPortfolio while taking the structure of {JSON_SCHEMA} into consideration.
    

<doc>Populate Detailed Idea Investment per team.</doc>
If {CT_DETAILED_IDEA_INVESTMENT_FILE} is not empty:

    Read out all hand-written post-its from {CT_DETAILED_IDEA_INVESTMENT_FILE}

    Map the extracted content to {TARGET_FILE}.container_DetailedIdeaInvestment while taking the structure of {JSON_SCHEMA} into consideration.


<doc>Populate Roadmap module.</doc>
If {MD_ROADMAP_FILE} is not empty:

    Read out all hand-written post-its from {MD_ROADMAP_FILE}

    Map the extracted content to {TARGET_FILE}.module_Roadmap while taking the structure of {JSON_SCHEMA} into consideration.


<doc>Populate Different Scenarios Rated by matching every handwritten score post-it to its scenario row and aspect column. Preserve the raw handwritten score in a PostIt while also storing a normalized numeric rating.</doc>
If {CT_DIFF_SCENARIOS_RATED_FILE} is not empty:

    Read out all hand-written post-its from {CT_DIFF_SCENARIOS_RATED_FILE}

    Map the extracted content to {TARGET_FILE}.container_DifferentScenariosRated while taking the structure of {JSON_SCHEMA} into consideration.

    Match each poster row to an existing Module_DifferentScenariosRated by its printed scenario label.

    Match each rating column to an existing ScenarioAspectRating by its printed aspect heading and category heading.

    For each handwritten score post-it in a matched scenario/aspect cell:

        Preserve the complete handwritten score text, including plus signs, minus signs, zeroes, slashes, and multiple stakeholder values.

        {NOTE_COUNTER} = {NOTE_COUNTER} + 1

        Create PostIt with:
            PostIt.id = {NOTE_COUNTER}
            PostIt.note = complete handwritten score text extracted from the post-it

        ScenarioAspectRating.explanation = PostIt

        If PostIt.note contains one numeric score:
            ScenarioAspectRating.rating = that numeric score

        Else if PostIt.note contains multiple stakeholder scores separated by a slash:
            ScenarioAspectRating.rating = arithmetic mean of all numeric scores on the post-it

        Do not populate PostIt.explanation during poster extraction. It is populated later from the scenario-specific workshop transcript.

<doc>Populate Scenario Summary module.</doc>
If {CT_SCENARIO_SUMMARY_FILE} is not empty:

    Read out all hand-written post-its from {CT_SCENARIO_SUMMARY_FILE}

    Map the extracted content to {TARGET_FILE}.container_ScenarioSummary while taking the structure of {JSON_SCHEMA} into consideration.
